4.	Greece has paid to June 30, 1920, as follows:	To Decmeber 1, 1919, $7,834.79;
to June 30, 1920, $53,160.61, being in full to that date. Interest account to December 31, 1920., amounting to $153,916.63, was rendered in due course and the Overseas Branch of the Department of Trade and Commerce, London, has now been able to present same to the Representative of the recently established Greek Government in London for payment. Roumania has made no payment of interest. Interest due to October 1st, 1920, amounted to $909,526.34 and on April 1, 1921, the total interest due will be $1,475,234.96. Accounts have been rendered. The question of the payment of this overdue interest and future interest instalments, has been the subject of negotiation between Representatives of the Dominion of Canada and the Kingdom of Roumania. These negotiations are still in progress.
